{
  "scope": "Finite open-ended channel and sliding bead: optional planar physical release experiment. Not a calibrated real ring-on-pin model.",
  "protocol": {
    "loadingStep": 0.0016666666666666668,
    "loading": "600 gravity steps; grip torso COM; 600 steps target(-4.3,297); 1200 steps target(pouch.x,pouch.y+0.85); drop; 300 settling steps; require isLoaded; clone canonical snapshot; unlatch and observe at most 5 seconds.",
    "units": "metres, seconds, kilograms; velocities are ragdoll center of mass at observed release. Each assembly changes its actual contact-loading history, so comparisons do not isolate release efficiency.",
    "channel": "One shared geometry in every variant: angle3.4rad relative arm, length0.22m, inner width0.07m, bead diameter0.05m/mass0.04kg, friction0.03. Closed heel and two finite rails; open tip. No slot joint, motor, release force, body velocity assignment, release-time fixture disabling or joint deletion.",
    "release": "Observe 0.01 seconds with no payload/cradle contact and center farther than0.7m from cradle. Hardware escape means bead center axial distance beyond channelLength+beadRadius; diagnostic only: rim ejection can occur before bead exit. Both straps and cradle persist.",
    "timestep": "Loading always1/600; only launch timestep changes."
  },
  "sourceSHA256": {
    "src/articulated.js": "fdce740ed84824f2c550ded7bf06a858d48d8155372e2d8ff4903e0609166575",
    "src/hook-experiment.js": "613a3f2b81459eecf870a56738c5de16ade7252500017931158693a3a3889ca4",
    "src/species.js": "156aaafe21f2b8203a9c1fce7dbda275c84266c73c4ed116d77a684934bbd35d"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Channel is a planar clevis abstraction rather than a closed3D ring.",
    "Release hardware collides only with matching hardware; massless straps do not collide with bodies.",
    "Rigid U cradle is retained; optional failed hinged-panel trials are recorded separately. Readiness uses the existing center-in-cradle envelope; it is not proof of settled load-bearing contact.",
    "Weak and backward shots remain possible; no per-species or per-shot tuning.",
    "Release detector observes later than exact last contact; it does not modify dynamics.",
    "Finite solver timestep/contact loss remains; no calibrated-realism claim.",
    "Baseline uses geometric ghost-cradle release and has different physical behavior."
  ],
